The helicopters were operated by two private companies, Fishtail Air and Dynasty Air.

In a statement, Fishtail Air said its helicopter was carrying passengers rescued from the Everest region when it crashed while landing.

googletag.cmd.push(function() { googletag.display("dfp-ad-tbs_rectangle_snd_mobile"); });

Both the Indian and New Zealand nationals on board were tourists, a Fishtail Air official said.

A Dynasty Air official said its helicopter was carrying only cargo at the time of the collision.

googletag.cmd.push(function() { googletag.display("dfp-ad-tbs_rectangle_snd_mobile02"); });

The accident occurred during Nepal's peak trekking season, when helicopters are frequently used to transport hikers and climbers across the region.

